DGEB EC classification (DNA) data — provenance
==============================================

Dataset : tattabio/ec_classification_dna  (HuggingFace)
Revision: cd61c74b4930cf9f1963e6d73ff7f14e2c8e74dd
License : DGEB benchmark, Apache-2.0 (repo TattaBio/DGEB). Underlying sequences are
          coding regions of UniProtKB "reviewed" entries (UniProt: CC BY 4.0).
Cite    : West-Roberts et al., "Diverse Genomic Embedding Benchmark for Functional
          Evaluation across the Tree of Life." bioRxiv 2024.07.10.602933.

640 protein-coding genes (DNA), each with a single Enzyme Commission (EC) class label.
128 EC classes; native HuggingFace splits: train (512 = 4 per class) / test (128 = 1 per
class). Source columns: Entry (UniProt accession), Sequence (CDS nucleotides), Label (EC).

gLMBench vendors, per split, a compact lowercase-header CSV (entry, sequence, label) where
``sequence`` is U→T/upper-normalized once at fetch time
(glmbench.tasks.dgeb_ec_data.preprocess_sequence). Sequence length ranges ~123 nt to
~14,700 nt (avg ~1.6–1.9 kb); over-context sequences are handled by the task's
window-and-mean (default) or truncate-central strategy — never silently dropped. The
heavy CSVs are gitignored; the sha256-pinned ``manifest.yaml`` + the committed tiny fixture
under ``tests/data/dgeb_ec_dna_tiny/`` make the integrity gate real.

Fetch (once, on a box with HuggingFace + ``datasets`` installed):
    python scripts/fetch_dgeb_ec_dna.py
